  "emoji": "🗣️",
  "summary": "Practise the speaking exam with a partner: introduce yourself, describe your city and family, ask the way and give your opinion, and keep the conversation going with بِبُطْء (slowly), هَلْ تَقْصِدُ…؟ (do you mean…?) and أَعْتَذِرُ (I apologise).",
  "intro": "In two days the final exam has a مُحَادَثَة (conversation) with a شَرِيك (partner), so today is speaking day. Nobody understands everything, and nobody speaks without mistakes; good speakers use strategies. If someone speaks too fast, ask politely: هَلْ تَسْتَطِيعُ أَنْ تَتَكَلَّمَ بِبُطْء؟ (could you speak slowly?) or أَرْجُو أَنْ تُكَرِّرَ السُّؤَال (please repeat the question). To check that you understood, say هَلْ تَقْصِدُ أَنَّ…؟ (do you mean that…?). To win a few seconds, say يَعْنِي… كَيْفَ أَقُولُ؟ (well… how can I put it?). And after a mistake, say أَعْتَذِرُ عَنْ هٰذَا الْخَطَأ or just عَفْوًا، أَقْصِدُ… (sorry, I mean…) and carry on. Today's verbs also have their own rhythm: نَطَقَ (na-ṭa-qa), عَبَّرَ (ʿab-ba-ra), حَاوَلَ (ḥā-wa-la).",
  "objectives": [
    "Introduce yourself and describe your city and family in a short speaking test",
    "Ask someone to repeat or to speak slowly with لَوْ سَمَحْتَ and أَرْجُو أَنْ…",
    "Check that you understood with هَلْ تَقْصِدُ أَنَّ…؟ and apologise for a mistake with أَعْتَذِرُ",
    "Give your opinion with فِي رَأْيِي and أَعْتَقِدُ أَنَّ, and use the words for conversation, accent, fluency and confidence"
  ],
