    "culture": "Arabic speakers fill pauses all the time, and the favourite filler is يَعْنِي (literally 'it means', here 'well…' or 'I mean'). In an exam it buys you a second or two, and it sounds natural. People are also very patient with learners: if you try to speak Arabic, even with an accent and a few mistakes, most people will be delighted and slow down for you. Every country has its own لَهْجَة (dialect and accent), but a clear, careful Standard Arabic is understood everywhere.",
